From: DolphinSlicer <build@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:25:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Model: no backup manager in the destructor under
 Emscripten

Loading a 3MF gives the model a backup folder (Model::get_backup_path()), and ~Model() hands
its removal to the autosave manager, whose constructor starts a thread. When the 3MF reader
throws (a truncated file), the model inside Model::read_from_file() is destroyed while the
exception unwinds; starting the thread fails in a single-threaded WebAssembly build, the
destructor throws and the program terminates instead of reporting the broken file.

There is no project autosave in the browser: under Emscripten remove the folder directly.

Upstreamable: no (WebAssembly only).
---
 src/libslic3r/Model.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libslic3r/Model.cpp b/src/libslic3r/Model.cpp
index d1265ccf..b243a464 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/Model.cpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/Model.cpp
@@ -235,8 +235,14 @@ Model::~Model()
     this->clear_objects();
     this->clear_materials();
     // BBS: clear backup dir of temparary model
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+    // No project autosave in the browser: remove the folder here instead of handing it to the
+    // backup manager, whose thread cannot be started from a destructor that must not throw.
+    try { this->remove_backup_path_if_exist(); } catch (...) {}
+#else
     if (!backup_path.empty())
         Slic3r::remove_backup(*this, true);
+#endif
 }
 
 Model Model::read_from_step(const std::string&                                      input_file,
